WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:16.428
the story, Onatah brought Magua a drink.

2
00:00:17.128 --> 00:00:18.429
He looked much better.

3
00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:21.550
"How many families live here?"

4
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.350
asked Mandy, looking around.

5
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:31.100
"Our longhouse has six families," said Onatah.

6
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.483
"I live with my grandmother, aunts, uncles, and cousins."

7
00:00:35.604 --> 00:00:37.045
A man entered the home.

8
00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:40.508
He whispered something to Clan Mother.

9
00:00:41.369 --> 00:00:42.970
She looked very serious.

10
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:50.056
"Onatah, take Vinnie and Mandy to the Green Corn dance," Clan Mother said.

11
00:00:50.076 --> 00:00:52.498
"What's wrong, Grandmother?"

12
00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:54.079
asked Onatah.

13
00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.121
"Don't worry.

14
00:00:56.561 --> 00:00:59.944
Go out and join the others," said Clan Mother.

15
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.021
"I will call you when I need you."

16
00:01:04.221 --> 00:01:06.202
The children left the longhouse.

17
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:11.865
"Everyone calls your grandmother 'Clan Mother,'" said Mandy.

18
00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:15.827
"Why?" "Women head all our families.

19
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.028
Women are wise," said Onatah.

20
00:01:19.048 --> 00:01:23.190
"People always come to my grandmother for advice.

21
00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.632
She is the oldest woman in our clan."

22
00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:31.333
Mandy thought of the other places she had visited.

23
00:01:32.494 --> 00:01:35.115
Men were always the most important ones.

24
00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:41.057
Among the Iroquois, women were more respected than men.

25
00:01:42.098 --> 00:01:45.039
Many people were gathered in the middle of the village.

26
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.120
Everyone looked excited.

27
00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:52.242
The dancers were dressed in colorful clothes.

28
00:01:54.263 --> 00:01:56.524
Some were holding feathers in their hands.

29
00:01:57.904 --> 00:01:59.605
Others wore them in their hair.

30
00:02:00.465 --> 00:02:03.426
People were singing and playing small drums.

31
00:02:03.446 --> 00:02:07.588
"We thank you for the harvest," people sang.

32
00:02:07.608 --> 00:02:09.609
"We planted.

33
00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:10.709
We gathered.

34
00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:11.730
We ate."

35
00:02:13.951 --> 00:02:18.313
The dancers pretended to plant corn, beans, and squash.

36
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:27.172
"Iroquois always plant the Three Sisters together in a small pile of soil," said Onatah.

37
00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:30.374
"And we use the shoulder blades of deer as hoes."

38
00:02:32.315 --> 00:02:34.556
Then Onatah jumped into the dance.

39
00:02:35.317 --> 00:02:37.038
Vinnie and Mandy did too.

40
00:02:38.699 --> 00:02:42.341
The rhythm of the loud drums matched the beat of their hearts.

41
00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:46.083
Everyone was smiling and laughing.

42
00:02:47.524 --> 00:02:50.565
After the dance, Onatah's grandmother spoke.

43
00:02:50.585 --> 00:02:55.088
"Something important has happened," said Clan Mother.

44
00:02:56.224 --> 00:02:58.045
"We must get ready for the council.

45
00:02:58.665 --> 00:02:59.405
They are coming."

46
00:03:00.866 --> 00:03:02.607
The people began to whisper.

47
00:03:02.627 --> 00:03:04.688
"The council?"

48
00:03:05.368 --> 00:03:06.148
asked Mandy.

49
00:03:06.168 --> 00:03:09.510
"Remember the story Grandmother told you?"

50
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.030
said Onatah.

51
00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:16.293
"Deganawidah chose fifty chiefs to look after the Iroquois.

52
00:03:17.453 --> 00:03:19.154
Each nation has ten chiefs.

53
00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:23.956
They come together to make important decisions for the Iroquois."

54
00:03:25.264 --> 00:03:27.185
Onatah looked at her grandmother.

55
00:03:28.026 --> 00:03:31.288
Clan Mother looked sadly at Vinnie and Mandy.

56
00:03:31.308 --> 00:03:33.469
"What is it?"

57
00:03:34.129 --> 00:03:34.890
asked Mandy.

58
00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:40.293
"The whites have come into our land," Clan Mother sighed.

59
00:03:40.313 --> 00:03:43.174
"A fight may begin soon."

60
00:03:44.495 --> 00:03:46.756
Vinnie and Mandy looked at each other.

61
00:03:46.776 --> 00:03:53.040
"Maybe we should call Deganawidah's name," said Vinnie.

62
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.201
"He promised to return."

63
00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:59.242
Clan Mother smiled and patted him lightly.

64
00:03:59.262 --> 00:04:02.444
"We will wait to hear from the council."

65
00:04:04.104 --> 00:04:06.505
Everyone stood near the central fire.

66
00:04:07.185 --> 00:04:08.426
People looked worried.

67
00:04:09.866 --> 00:04:12.187
No one danced or laughed anymore.

68
00:04:12.207 --> 00:04:14.989
"When are the chiefs coming?"

69
00:04:15.609 --> 00:04:17.049
asked Mandy nervously.

70
00:04:17.069 --> 00:04:18.850
"Will it be soon?"

71
00:04:20.011 --> 00:04:21.331
No one answered her.
